% Generate `server/settings.py`: local user preferences for the packaged desktop app — small JSON
% values that are NOT secrets (secrets live in the BYOK `.env`). Module-level functions, no class.
% `from __future__ import annotations`. Import json, os, tempfile, uuid; `Path`; typing `Any`; and
% `from lib import app_paths`.

% Design contract (state in the module docstring): prefs are stored as one JSON object at
% `<app_paths.home()>/settings.json`, so they sit next to the user's data (App Support in the
% packaged app, repo root in dev) and never inside the read-only bundle. Reads must NEVER raise —
% a missing OR corrupt file must fall back to defaults, never brick the backend. Writes are ATOMIC:
% serialize to a temp file in the same directory, fsync, then `os.replace`, so a crash or a
% concurrent reader never sees a half-written file.

## Constants
- `_DEFAULTS: dict[str, Any] = {"analytics_disabled": False}` — analytics is opt-OUT (on by default;
  `False` = allowed). This is the only baked-in default; everything else is written on demand.

## API
- `read_all() -> dict` — `_DEFAULTS` overlaid with whatever is on disk. If the file is missing,
  unreadable, non-JSON, or not a JSON object, return the defaults (swallow `JSONDecodeError`/`OSError`);
  only a dict from disk overlays the defaults.
- `get(key, default=None) -> Any` — `read_all().get(key, default)`.
- `set_value(key, value) -> dict` — read current, set the one key, write atomically, return the full
  post-write dict.
- `device_id() -> str` — a stable, anonymous per-install id for analytics (NO PII): `dev-<uuid4 hex>`,
  generated once and persisted (via `set_value`) so it is reused across launches; consumed by
  `server.analytics`.

## Helpers
- `_path()` = `app_paths.home() / "settings.json"`.
- `_write_atomic(data)` — `mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` the parent, `tempfile.mkstemp` in that
  same dir (so `os.replace` is atomic on one filesystem), `json.dump(indent=2)` then flush + `os.fsync`,
  then `os.replace(tmp, path)`. On ANY `BaseException`, unlink the temp file (ignore unlink errors) and
  re-raise.
